    <!--
        ===== Prometheus Java Client (io.prometheus:simpleclient) =====

        CVE-2026-42154 (CVSS 7.5): Reported against simpleclient 0.16.0.
        The simpleclient 0.x series reached end-of-life at 0.16.0; no
        patched 0.x release exists. Migrating to the Prometheus 1.x API
        (io.prometheus:prometheus-metrics-core) would require a Micrometer
        version bump beyond what Spring Boot 3.2.x manages and is out of
        scope for this release cycle.

        Risk acceptance rationale:
          - The /actuator/prometheus scrape endpoint is restricted to the
            internal monitoring network (Prometheus server only) and is
            not exposed to public traffic.
          - The dashboard pipeline is internal-only with no untrusted
            external input reaching the simpleclient metrics registry.
          - Attack surface is limited to metric label injection, which is
            mitigated by Micrometer's label sanitisation layer.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes>CVE-2026-42154 (7.5): simpleclient 0.16.0 is end-of-life; no
            patched 0.x release. Prometheus scrape endpoint is
            internal-network-only; risk accepted for internal dashboard use.
        </notes>
        <cve>CVE-2026-42154</cve>
    </suppress>

